  "sections": [
    {
      "key": "quickFacts",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/25-perchlike-fishes/25e-perchlike-fishes-5-remaining-cichlids-from-south-and-central-america/cichla_orinocensis_en/",
      "html": "<ul><li>Origin: Venezuela</li><li>Maturity is usually reached at a length of 20-25 cm</li></ul>"
    },
    {
      "key": "diet",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/25-perchlike-fishes/25e-perchlike-fishes-5-remaining-cichlids-from-south-and-central-america/cichla_orinocensis_en/",
      "html": "<p>Youngsters can be fed with white mosquito larvae and bloodworm; however, feeder fish are ideal. From a size of about 10 cm on, the young Cichla can be fed with frozen smelt as the basic food. Smelt can be used even for the largest specimens.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "dimorphism",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/25-perchlike-fishes/25e-perchlike-fishes-5-remaining-cichlids-from-south-and-central-america/cichla_orinocensis_en/",
      "html": "<p>One can observe the unique sexual dichromatism of Cichla orinocensis: males look rather like Cichla ocellaris, while females have a colour pattern that reminds one of C. temensis.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "reproduction",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/25-perchlike-fishes/25e-perchlike-fishes-5-remaining-cichlids-from-south-and-central-america/cichla_orinocensis_en/",
      "html": "<p>All species of Cichla are, as far as it is known, openbrooders and perform bipartental broodcare.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "notes",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/25-perchlike-fishes/25e-perchlike-fishes-5-remaining-cichlids-from-south-and-central-america/cichla_orinocensis_en/",
      "html": "<p>Cichla: a name used in ancient Greece for a fish that is unknown today. orinocensis: means \"originating from the Rio Orinoco\".</p>"
    }
  ],
